# direnv entry point for the simdjson Zig SDK.
#
# `devenv` is the canonical development environment for this SDK: devenv.nix
# defines it and devenv.yaml pins its one input. This file does nothing except
# hand a shell that already has direnv over to it. It defines no environment
# variable, no path and no cache location of its own -- the scratch and cache
# policy belongs to the environment this shell is entered from, and to
# devenv.nix's own resolution of it at shell entry.
#
# In particular nothing here names a store path. simdjson's On-Demand API is
# exception-free, so `-fno-exceptions -fno-rtti` plus Zig's bundled libc++ is
# the intended C++ route and this SDK needs no external WASI SDK sysroot the way
# s2geometry does; that is why there is no sysroot to export here and nothing
# this file could usefully add.
#
# Nothing here is required. `devenv shell` alone is enough, and it is the
# supported path; this is a convenience for a direnv-enabled shell.
#
# direnv is not installed by this repository. If it is missing, the shell says
# so rather than falling back to something else in a directory that looks
# configured and is not.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

if ! has devenv; then
  echo "simdjson: devenv is not on PATH; this repository's development shell is entered with 'devenv shell', or by installing direnv." >&2
  return 1
fi

use devenv